'''Occidental Province''' was the Sartan province created from the return of the coastal territories in the [[Occidental Agreement of 1846]]. It covered the restored western coastal lands that had previously been under Volisanian control.

The province was part of the territorial settlement that followed the post-1811 constitutional order. Its creation returned Sarta to the coast, but it also tied the kingdom more closely to Volisania through the coal concession attached to the agreement.

Occidental Province remained one of the key symbols of the nineteenth-century compromise between recovery and dependence. In Sartan political writing, it was often treated less as a new creation than as the formal restoration of lands that had been lost after the [[Second Sartan Civil War]].

== History ==

The province emerged from the [[Occidental Agreement of 1846]], which ended the long dispute over Sarta's coastal territories. Anti-Volisanian critics called the settlement the [[Tontas Trato]], but the province itself became the administrative label for the returned lands.

